          %hr/
          %h1#20090131 2009-01-31
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    Created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
                    and
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
                %li
                  %p
                    Clarified homotopy limits at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+2-category"} model 2-category
                    and
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  created
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+2-category"} model 2-category
                  and tried to subsume our discussion about it at
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
                  – would like ask
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike
                  to check
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"} Ronnie Brown
              %ul
                %li
                  created
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+algebra"} higher dimensional algebra
          %h1#20090130 2009-01-30
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    added more examples to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span+trace"} span trace
                    (see
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/01/benzvi_on_geometric_function_t.html#c021787"} blog comment
                %li
                  %p
                    added
                    %em based loop object
                    to
                    %em free loop object
                    at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
                    and linked that with
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"}> Tim
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Continued work on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+n-cube"} crossed n-cube
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
          %h1#20090129 2009-01-29
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    Finally decided I need to get over my Australian training and make weak things the default, at least when writing on the nLab. So I split up
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categorical+limit"} 2-categorical limit
                    into
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
                    for the weak notion and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
                    for the strict one. The exposition here could probably use help, and I have a question about terminology for
                    = succeed "s." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
                %li
                  %p
                    Redirected
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray+category"} Gray category
                    to the already-existing
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray-category"} Gray-category
                %li
                  %p
                    I haven’t done much here recently because I’ve been working in my
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/HomePage"} own web
                    on a project developing
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/2-categorical+logic"} 2-categorical logic
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Forgy"}> Eric
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  changed yet
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} another definition
                  from
                  %em italic
                  to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %strong bold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"}> David
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Added a remark after Urs’ remark on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophy
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"}> Tim
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    Continued work on
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+n-cube"} crossed n-cube
                    and related entries.
                %li
                  %p
                    Linked the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
                    to the entry on the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                    where there was already some discussion of this topic.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    have a question/request at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
                    about “homotopical enrichment”. Can anyone say more about this?
                    = succeed "?" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timothy+Porter"} Tim
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
                    and included at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span+trace"} span trace
                    as an example the statement that the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
                    is the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy trace
                    of the identity span on the object
                %li
                  %p
                    have a request at the end of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categorical+limit"} 2-categorical limit
                    that we eventually give a formulation in terms of
                    = succeed "s." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
                %li
                  %p
                    added the defintiion in terms of adjoints to the constant diagram functor to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                %li
                  %p
                    replied to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Forgy"} Eric
                    at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
                    and also
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+theorem"} Dold-Kan theorem
                    as a redirect
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
                %li
                  %p
                    have a remark/question at one point in
                    = succeed "\u2018s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"} David
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophy
                %li
                  %p
                    started giving a discussion of the point of (higher) category theory in
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
          %h1#20090128 2009-01-28
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"} Ronnie Brown
              %ul
                %li
                  created/worked on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cat-n-group"} cat-n-group
                  = succeed "," do
